---

This license covers the port's own code: the build and packaging scripts, the
drivers, the patches under `patches/`, and the documentation.

It does NOT cover the third-party components a built VPK bundles, each of which
keeps its own terms:

- **the Gen1Recomp engine, packed into `game.love`: GPL-3.0 with Additional
  Terms under Section 7**, Copyright (C) 2026 BOIS CLUB GAMES, LLC. An earlier
  version of this file wrongly called it MIT. Read the engine's own `LICENSE.MD`
  before redistributing anything containing it. Two terms matter most:
  - **Term 1** requires visible credit in the README and in any in-app credits,
    title screen, launcher or front end, reading at minimum "Based on the Pokemon
    Gen 1 Recompilation Project by BOIS CLUB GAMES, LLC
    (https://github.com/bryanthaboi/gen1recomp)".
  - **Term 2** makes the Launcher proprietary and all rights reserved, and
    permits distributing it with the program "only in unmodified official
    releases from BOIS CLUB GAMES, LLC". A built VPK contains it, so a
    third-party Vita build cannot be distributed as a playable artifact.
- LOVE 11.x (zlib), built from the `love-vita` tree with the patches here. Its
  eboot statically links **mpg123 and OpenAL Soft, both LGPL-2.1**, which carries
  a relink or source obligation on anyone distributing a built binary.
- LuaJIT (MIT)
- PowerVR `PVR_PSP2` GPU modules and `libGL.suprx` from `gl4es4vita`, which the
  build fetches rather than vendoring. These are repackaged proprietary GPU
  drivers; nothing found grants redistribution, which is a further reason this
  repo ships no binary.

No ROM or ROM-derived data is included in this repository or in a built VPK.
The player supplies their own. Pokemon and all related names and content are the
property of Nintendo, Creatures Inc., and GAME FREAK inc.
